# program cc_i2c_nack  (262 image bytes)
# source: ~/Documents/protocol-emulator/test/cocotb_tests/protocols.py:i2c_write_then_read
# I2C at 100 kHz, SCL uio2 SDA uio3, open drain. Addresses 0x3A,
# where nothing answers: the first RX entry (the address ACK bit) must be 1 = NACK.
# On the board this needs only the pull-ups (internal ones suffice at 100 kHz).

test absent_address_is_nacked
reset
drain 1
loop 00000000
cmds 
rx 0 1 100000 01
end
